  "review": {
    "review": "The hero died to lightning: decision 3621's accepted transition (log line 10437) records health falling from two to zero and explicitly reports a fatal lightning bolt. The initiating defect investigated is earlier: decision 3609 (line 10391) abandons a wall-separated position to seek a remembered door merely because a DM-100 is visible. An isolated original-helper probe on the recorded public input reproduces step 964 and the reported door plan, although both conservative bolt-line checks find the hero occluded. This is not a full reconstruction of original runtime memory. The proposed guard declines new door flight without current or remembered exposure, leaving existing controllers to choose any subsequent action. A new deterministic public-geometry regression fails as expected on the original selector and passes after correction; the candidate full suite passes 1,929 tests with four skips. This does not establish a safe replacement action or survival, and no changed trajectory was replayed.",
